  "schema": 1,
  "note": "The on-screen control hints shown during play (docs/ui/hud-spec.md section 22) and the YOU labels. One scheme per control layout, named by the layout's id in data/input/layouts.json (kb-solo, kb-shared-p1, kb-shared-p2, arena, simple-pad); the HUD picks the scheme from the player's device and preset and falls back to 'today'. A row is an action (or a group) and a short word; the glyph drawn is the active layout's own binding for that action (the keys or buttons Controls wrote in layouts.json), so a remap shows the player's own controls. A row for an action the layout does not bind is skipped. A row with only_when_avail shows only while the fighter can use that action (Transform, while a form is ready). The touch layout has no legend: its buttons are on screen. intro_seconds: how long the hints show at the start of every match (the last two seconds fade) unless prompts are on or the control_hints option is always.",
